1
00:03:43,199 --> 00:03:49,199
Hunt or be hunted.

2
00:07:26,399 --> 00:07:32,399
Hunter Hunter is a horror, thriller, mystery film directed by Shawn Linden.

3
00:11:09,599 --> 00:11:15,599
A fur trapper leaves his wife and daughter behind to kill a rogue wolf in the remote wilderness, but
they soon become increasingly worried when their peaceful existence is disrupted.

4
00:14:52,799 --> 00:14:58,799
Anne Mersault, played by Camille Sullivan.

5
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Renee Mersault, played by Summer H. Howell.

6
00:22:19,199 --> 00:22:25,199
Joseph Mersault, played by Devon Sawa.

7
00:26:02,399 --> 00:26:08,399
Lou, played by Nick Stahl.

8
00:29:45,599 --> 00:29:51,599
Danny Barthes, played by Gabriel Daniels.

9
00:33:28,799 --> 00:33:34,799
Lucy, played by Lauren Cochrane.

10
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Hunter × Hunter (pronounced "hunter hunter") is a Japanese manga
series written and illustrated by Yoshihiro Togashi.

11
00:40:55,199 --> 00:41:01,199
It has been serialized in Shueisha's shōnen manga magazine Weekly Shōnen Jump since March
1998, although the manga has frequently gone on extended hiatuses since 2006.

12
00:44:38,399 --> 00:44:44,399
Its chapters have been collected in 38 tankōbon volumes as of September 2024.

13
00:48:21,599 --> 00:48:27,599
The story focuses on a young boy named Gon Freecss who discovers that his father, who left him at a young age, is actually a world-renowned Hunter, a licensed professional who
specializes in fantastical pursuits such as locating rare or unidentified animal species, treasure hunting, surveying unexplored enclaves, or hunting down lawless individuals.

14
00:52:04,799 --> 00:52:10,799
Gon departs on a journey to become a Hunter and eventually find his father.

15
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
Along the way, Gon meets various other Hunters and encounters the paranormal.

16
00:59:31,199 --> 00:59:37,199
Hunter × Hunter was adapted into a 62-episode anime television series by Nippon Animation and directed
by Kazuhiro Furuhashi, which ran on Fuji Television from October 1999 to March 2001.

17
01:03:14,399 --> 01:03:20,399
Three separate original video animations (OVAs) totaling 30 episodes were subsequently
produced by Nippon Animation and released in Japan from 2002 to 2004.

18
01:06:57,599 --> 01:07:03,599
A second anime television series by Madhouse aired on Nippon Television from October 2011 to
September 2014, totaling 148 episodes, with two animated theatrical films released in 2013.

19
01:10:40,800 --> 01:10:46,800
There are also numerous audio albums, video games, musicals,
and other media based on Hunter × Hunter.

20
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
The manga has been licensed for English release in North
America by Viz Media since April 2005.

21
01:18:07,199 --> 01:18:13,199
Both television series have been also licensed by Viz Media, with the first series having aired on the Funimation Channel in
2009 and the second series broadcast on Adult Swim's Toonami programming block from April 2016 to June 2019.

22
01:21:50,399 --> 01:21:56,399
Hunter × Hunter has been widely acclaimed and commercially successful, becoming one of the best-selling
manga series of all time with over 84 million copies in circulation worldwide by July 2022.

23
01:25:33,599 --> 01:25:39,599
The film explores themes of canada, husband wife
relationship, wolf, wilderness, fur trapping.

24
01:29:16,799 --> 01:29:22,799
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
